  "goodToKnow": "Die Kirchengemeinde is a parish or congregation, the local community of a church: die evangelische Kirchengemeinde. On its own, die Gemeinde also means a municipality, so the full compound avoids confusion. Kirchengemeinden run kindergartens, choirs and youth groups, funded partly by the Kirchensteuer that registered members pay. Das Gemeindehaus is the parish hall, and der Gemeinderat can be either council."
